      "content": "If you wish to explore heightened sensory awareness, controlled sensory reduction, like meditation or floatation therapy, can help minimize external stimuli. Try setting aside specific blocks of time in complete quiet, perhaps using noise-canceling headphones in an otherwise dark room. However, be mindful that intentionally intensifying sensory focus can also be overwhelming, so start slowly and prioritize maintaining a sense of comfort and safety. Always listen to your body and know when to stop if the intensity becomes distressing.",
